# What reaches `docker build`.
#
# THIS is the file docker reads for the web image. `web/Dockerfile` is built
# with the repository root as its context — the server is a front end over
# `bin/report-maker`, so the engine has to be in the context — and docker takes
# its ignore file from the context root, never from the Dockerfile's directory.
# `web/.dockerignore` exists as a mirror for anyone who builds with `web/` as
# the context; it has no effect on the build this repository ships.

# Version control and editor litter.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.devcontainer
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp

# Generated. Every one of these is rebuilt from source, and shipping a stale
# copy into an image is how a container ends up serving something no commit
# describes.
out/
.build/
**/out/
**/.build/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/node_modules/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
web/client/dist/

# The desktop app. Same engine, different front end; nothing in the server
# reaches for it.
app/

# The demo vault. A session vault is seeded by `report-maker init` and
# `report-maker new`, which read `engine/templates/` — not this folder.
examples/

# The engine suite. It is not run inside the runtime image; a contributor runs
# `make test` in a checkout or in the devcontainer.
tests/
web/tests/

# Deployment descriptors for other targets, and prose. None of it is code the
# server runs.
docker-compose.yml
web/fly.toml
web/render.yaml
audits/

# Prose. Nothing the image COPYs is markdown, and `**` is spelled out because a
# bare `*.md` matches only the root — docker's patterns do not cross `/` on a
# single star, which is the sort of detail that quietly ships a 37 KB README.
**/*.md
